    "title": "Percentage of missed votes by members of Congress from Wisconsin in 2023-24 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago In the last complete congressional term of 2023-2024, U.S. Rep Gwen Moore, a Democrat from Milwaukee, had the highest absentee rate, at 6.4%,according to data from GovTrack. Rep. Mark Pocan, a Democrat from Madison, was next at 4.4%. That puts Moore in the top 15% of most missed votes in the 435-member House, and Pocan just inside the top 25%. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
